 ### [Aggregated Bidirectional Scattering Distribution Function (ABSDF)](13367-aggregated-bidirectional-scattering-distribution-function-ab.md)
-The Aggregated Bidirectional Scattering Distribution Function (ABSDF) is a method for efficient scene appearance aggregation for Level-of-Detail (LoD) rendering, designed to handle scenes with high geometric complexity and instancing. It defines a 4D function of incident and outgoing directions that describes the far-field appearance of a scene aggregate by integrating the 8D light transport function over positions, effectively capturing the aggregated appearance of all surfaces within a volume. Unlike explicit geometry rendering, ABSDF precomputes aggregated visibility and material properties, allowing the renderer to avoid tracing explicit geometry and shadow rays, thereby reducing the sample count required for convergence. It builds on Aggregated Microfacet Distribution Approximation by providing a closed-form factorization that supports all-frequency and view-dependent effects.
+The Aggregated Bidirectional Scattering Distribution Function (ABSDF) is a method for efficient scene appearance aggregation for Level-of-Detail (LoD) rendering, designed to handle scenes with high geometric complexity and instancing. It defines a 4D function of incident and outgoing directions that describes the far-field appearance of a scene aggregate by integrating the 8D light transport function over positions, effectively capturing the aggregated appearance of all surfaces within a volume. Unlike explicit geometry rendering, ABSDF precomputes aggregated visibility and material properties, allowing the renderer to avoid tracing explicit geometry and shadow rays, thereby reducing the sample count required for convergence. It builds on [Aggregated Microfacet Distribution Approximation](10880-aggregated-microfacet-distribution-approximation.md) by providing a closed-form factorization that supports all-frequency and view-dependent effects. See [Aggregated Bidirectional Scattering Distribution Function (ABSDF)](13367-aggregated-bidirectional-scattering-distribution-function-ab.md).
