+### [Horizon Principled BRDF](14801-horizon-principled-brdf.md)
+The Horizon Principled BRDF is a bidirectional reflectance distribution function used in the Horizon rendering engine, designed to be compatible with Disney's principled shading approach. It solves the problem of providing a physically plausible, energy-conserving shading model that supports a wide range of material types (dielectric, metallic, clear coat, sheen) through a unified set of normalized parameters. It sets itself apart from its parent, Aggregated Microfacet Distribution Approximation, by fixing specific parameter values (such as $\gamma=2$ for the main lobe and $\gamma=1$ for clear coat) and implementing a specific diffuse Fresnel variation to correct edge darkening, rather than using a general aggregation function. See [Horizon Principled BRDF](14801-horizon-principled-brdf.md).
 
